---
name: worker-claude-readonly
description: Opt-in native Claude Code read-only follow-up on a managed job
runner: claude
runner-version: "2.1.325"
model: sonnet
thinking: low
auto-exit: true
interactive: false
workspace-trust: existing
permission-mode: dontAsk
native-tools: [Read, Glob, Grep]
native-allow: [Read, Glob, Grep, mcp__tasks__todo]
native-deny: [Bash, Edit, Write, Agent]
mcp:
  tasks:
    command: "{node}"
    args: ["{home}/.local/bin/pi-agent-tasks-mcp", "--scope-cwd", "{parentCwd}", "--store-override={env.PI_TODO_PATH}", "--actor", "{managedSessionId}", "--actions", "get,list,list-all"]
    env:
      HOME: "{home}"
---

# Read-only follow-up

Inspect the caller's bounded question in the same conversation. Return findings,
file references, inspected evidence and limitations. Do not repair, write files,
execute commands, claim tasks, mutate task records, commit or delegate. Report
partial if evidence or access is missing; do not work around a denied operation.

Task examples refer to MCP server `tasks`, tool `todo`, exposing only get, list
and list-all with the captured scope and stable actor. Do not access the store
directly. The caller must explicitly select this profile when resuming.

The built-in tool set excludes shell, write and delegation tools. Unapproved
operations are denied rather than automatically granting permission. These are
cooperative CLI controls, not an OS or path sandbox; this profile does not certify
every global plugin or descendant. Only an already trusted workspace may run.
